WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.534
-Charli,
welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.667
You look fantastic. Thank you
so much for coming back.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:05.667
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:06.968
-The first time
you were here,

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:09.167
I want to say, it was three
and a half years ago

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:11.767
or something like that,
and we were talking.

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:15.133
We're both excited because
you had 32 million followers

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:17.033
and on TikTok, and it was like,
"Wow, that's awesome."

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:18.334
Here we are.

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:20.534
That's not that long ago,
three and a half years ago,

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:23.200
you're at 151 million followers.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:26.868
Is that crazy?

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:29.467
-I mean, to me,
it's like, I can --

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:32.567
Like, this is a lot of people,
and I get so nervous.

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:34.167
So to think that I actually post

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.667
for that many people
is absolutely insane.

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:38.834
-Yeah.

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.200
-I can't really
understand it,

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.901
but I feel like
it's better that way,

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:43.767
because I can be less nervous.

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:47.267
-Yeah. Well, how old are you
when you first started?

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:49.300
-I was 15.
-15.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.367
-On the show last time,
I was 15.

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:52.167
-Good for you, buddy.
That's so tough.

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:53.968
I mean, you stayed strong.

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:56.234
I mean, that must be
a lot of pressure, you know,

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:58.200
to start a business
and keep going and

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.501
and keep thinking of new ideas.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:01.667
And then you have the show,

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:03.567
and now your whole family
is involved now.

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:06.267
Do you ever go back
and watch your old TikToks?

00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:08.767
-I do and I make fun
of myself a lot

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:11.000
because it is so embarrassing.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.133
But it's also fun
to go down memory lane

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:15.434
and be like, "Oh, my goodness,
this outfit was atrocious,

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:16.567
but, look, it was so cute.

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:17.868
I was a baby."

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:20.000
-Yeah, yeah. You still are.
You still are.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.300
I wanted to ask you something,
because I saw "Vanity Fair."

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.300
They did a thing.
You did a lie-detector test.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.067
You know what I'm about to say?
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.834
-Yeah, you love Dunkin' Donuts.
-I do.

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:31.234
-Okay, well, let's just watch
this lie-detector test.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.300
-Do you actually like Dunkin'
as much as you say you do?

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.367
-Yes, and I shamelessly
promote them so much.

00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:38.300
No, I'm such a fan
of Dunkin' Donuts.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.801
-I'm happy that they're doing,
like, cool stuff, though.

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:44.133
-Do you think you like Dunkin'
more than this person?

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:45.234
-Yes.

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:46.934
-Do you know who that is?
-No.

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:48.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:51.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:55.033
-You don't know
who Ben Affleck is?

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:57.033
-No, I do,
and I've, like, fully had

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:58.567
conversations with him before.

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:01.534
And, like, I know who --
That's why it's so unb--

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:03.534
My sister clowned me
for that so hard

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:05.234
the entire ride back.

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:08.634
I was so embarrassed.
-But that's hilarious.

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:09.801
So like, "Yeah, I love --"

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:10.901
"You like it better
than this person?"

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:12.133
And you just blanked?

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:14.334
-Because I just, like --
I know how much --

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.534
I've had two coffees
already today, you know?

00:02:16.534 --> 00:02:17.701
Like, I --
-Yes.

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:19.400
You were in the zone
of Dunkin' Donuts.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:22.234
-I know how much I love it,
and it's more than...

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:23.267
-Anyone.
-...anyone.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:24.400
-Yeah, including that person

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:25.634
who, at the time,
you didn't know.

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:27.400
-Now I've looked
at the photos,

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.634
I feel like we can be equal.

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:32.334
-Oh, my God. That's so funny.

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:33.801
You were telling me
backstage, though,

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:35.868
that you actually had a great
meeting with Jennifer Lopez...

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:37.133
-Yeah.

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:38.667
-...who is like --
Gosh, we have that in common.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:40.267
She is unbelievable.
We both love Jennifer Lopez.

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:43.467
-I love her.
She was the absolute sweetest.

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:45.801
Every single time
I've spoken to her,

00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:48.000
she, like,
can see inside my brain

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.834
and tell me exactly
what I need to hear

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:51.067
without even knowing.

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:54.834
Like, genuinely,
my dream when I was younger

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:56.367
was to be
a backup dancer for her.

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:57.968
That was all that
I ever wanted in life.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:03:00.200
-Me too.
-I'm such a fan.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.701
We still can.
-We still can, yeah.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:04.767
Jennifer, if you're watching,
we're in. Yeah.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:07.100
-If you need us.
-She is just the best, right?

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.567
She is a pro.

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:11.267
When she comes on the show,
I mean, she -- Her in concert.

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:13.634
Go -- If she tours again --
Well, she will.

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:15.100
-But --
-She's insane.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.467
-A professional.
She puts the work in, man.

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:19.200
-It's incredible.
-Yeah.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.567
I know Halloween is coming up,

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.667
and you're a big fan
of Halloween.

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:24.601
Can you say what
you're dressing up as? No?

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:27.634
-I have, like, a list,
quite a long list,

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:30.601
in my notes of --
I work on it all year long,

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:32.901
add to it every week, you know?

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:36.734
But, so far, I only have
like one or two locked down.

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:38.300
I want to do Boo
from "Monsters, Inc.",

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.701
because I have the bob,
and I feel like it

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:41.100
just kind of works, you know?

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.334
-Okay. That's good.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:46.167
-But, I mean, my boyfriend
and I were trying to do,

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:48.734
like, cute couples costumes,
but we're so indecisive

00:03:48.734 --> 00:03:51.334
that we just, like,
can't actually get it together.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:52.701
-Yeah.
-We have time.

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:55.501
-You do have a little time.
Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.534
You have like a --
Yeah, you have like a week.

00:03:57.534 --> 00:04:00.734
You don't really have time,
to really be honest.

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:02.267
Your career
has actually blown up.

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:03.767
It's so cool to watch on TikTok.

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:05.667
Now you turn it into
a business now.

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:07.634
You have a shoe line.

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:09.367
Talk about this.
How fun is that?

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:11.567
-It's crazy. I mean,
all I really know about shoes

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:13.634
is the fact
that I wear them every day,

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:15.734
so I don't know
how it actually works,

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:17.567
but we have such an amazing team
behind us

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:19.968
that can, you know --
We're in heels a lot.

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.968
There's three girls
in the family.

00:04:21.968 --> 00:04:24.901
We're all constantly, like,
blisters, everything hurts.

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:28.334
So it's been really fun to take
my favorite parts of shoes

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:31.234
and my least favorite parts of
shoes and work it all together

00:04:31.234 --> 00:04:33.234
and make them comfortable,
stylish, cute,

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:34.767
get to pick the colors,
the shapes,

00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:36.067
the silhouettes, the styles.

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:37.801
So it's really fun.
-I mean, you have everything.

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:39.200
You have, like --
You have slides.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.534
You have sneakers.
I'm like, it's so --

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:43.100
Actually,
you wore them in today.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.634
I was like, "You should just
wear them out with your dress.

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:45.767
Why not?"

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:48.133
They're, like --
They're cute sneakers.

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:51.000
But that's wild that you go,
"Yeah, I had this idea

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.367
and I'm going to make it real."

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:54.267
And you're making
all this stuff a reality.

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:56.100
-I know. It's insane.
-I'm so happy for you, buddy.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.234
-Thank you!
-Really. I'm a big...

00:04:58.234 --> 00:04:59.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:02.601
And the show,
"The D'Amelio Show,"

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:03.934
is streaming on Hulu.

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:05.701
-Yes.
-How is the family holding up?

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.167
How's the parents?

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:10.434
Are they going -- Yeah, is it
going to their head, the fame?

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:14.567
-You know, the fam is good.
We are together a lot.

00:05:14.567 --> 00:05:15.968
It's great.

00:05:15.968 --> 00:05:18.501
I mean, I live with my older
sister and we work together,

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:20.968
so we spend quite
a lot of time together.

00:05:20.968 --> 00:05:23.601
You know, sisters -- we argue,
but we love each other.

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:25.701
-A lot of family bonding.
-Yeah. A lot.

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:27.634
-Yeah. We love it every time
you come by.

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:29.334
Thank you so much,
and congrats on the show

00:05:29.334 --> 00:05:30.501
and on the shoes, as well.

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:32.567
-Thank you!
-Charli D'Amelio, everybody.

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:37.567
Season 3 of "The D'Amelio Show"
is streaming now on Hulu.

00:05:37.567 --> 00:05:39.968
Victoria Monét
performs for us after the break.

00:05:39.968 --> 00:05:41.133
Stick around, everybody.

